{
  "$comment": [
    "The nine product entities and the shared kernel of edge8-web, as decided in",
    "docs/engineering/2026-09-03-multi-entity-design.md. Every path in the tree resolves",
    "to exactly one owner by longest-prefix match over `current` and `target`; an entry",
    "without a file extension also matches that stem's .ts/.tsx/.test.ts siblings.",
    "Since ME-13 `current` equals `[target]` for every owner: all code lives under",
    "entities/<name>/ or kernel/, and app/ is the composition root (\"app\"), a tree of",
    "thin mounts that re-export entity routes, api handlers and crons.",
    "scripts/gen-entity-zones.mjs turns this file into the ESLint boundary zones and",
    "scripts/check-entity-imports.mjs fails any cross-entity import that is not a door.",
    "`tables` lists the Supabase tables and views each owner writes (design \u00a74, then the",
    "reader with the most call sites for tables the design does not name). Only the owner",
    "writes a table directly; scripts/check-table-ownership.mjs ratchets cross-entity reads",
    "and fails cross-entity writes. A few names (trip_*, private_session_blocks,",
    "brand_contacts, requisition_loop_interviewers) are absent from the generated types",
    "but still read by code, so they carry an owner too.",
    "`layer` orders the entities (the kernel is 0): an entity's doors, and everything they reach inside the entity, may import another entity's doors only when that entity has a strictly lower layer, so the door graph is a DAG by construction. Route bodies, api/ and crons/ are the mounts app/ composes and are exempt. scripts/check-entity-layers.mjs enforces it (Q2)."
  ],
